# PART 3 — FIVE FOUNDATIONAL FINANCE TASKS

# Task 21 — First-Time Finance Setup and Opening Balances

## Objective

Allow the user to establish their actual starting financial position.

### 21.1 First-time setup

When the user first enters Finance, check whether initial setup has been completed.

If not, guide the user through the necessary setup.

Collect:

- The user's actual name, if it has not already been collected during global app onboarding.
- The financial accounts they use.
- The opening balance of each account.

Do not assume the user's name or invent financial values.

### 21.2 Default accounts

Provide these initial account options:

- CBE
- BOA
- Dashen Bank
- Telebirr
- Cash

The user must be able to add additional accounts.

The user should not be forced to use every default account.

### 21.3 Opening balances

For every selected account:

- Allow the user to enter its actual starting balance.
- Allow zero as a valid balance.
- Do not automatically populate nonzero balances.
- Clearly identify which balance belongs to which account.
- Use the application's existing currency conventions.

The user should be able to review all entered information before completing setup.

### 21.4 Opening balance dates

Store an appropriate opening-balance date for each account.

The opening balance represents money already available when financial tracking begins.

It must not be counted as income or a salary transaction.

### 21.5 Saving setup

- Validate all entered information.
- Prevent accidental duplicate setup.
- Save accounts and opening balances persistently.
- Complete setup only after successful database persistence.
- Preserve user input if saving fails.
- Display understandable error messages.
- Navigate to the simplified Finance dashboard after successful setup.

### Acceptance Tests

1. First-time setup appears when appropriate.
2. Completed setup does not unnecessarily appear again.
3. The user can select the accounts they actually use.
4. The user can add another account.
5. Each account accepts its own opening balance.
6. Zero balances are accepted.
7. No invented balances or dummy transactions appear.
8. Opening balances are not counted as income.
9. Setup persists after restarting the app.
10. Failed setup does not leave partially initialized data.

